Dependent Packages
==================

The NEMO3D application is dependent on the following freely available
external packages:

PYTHON     : Scripting Interpreter
BLAS       : Basic Linear Algebra Fortran Library
             http://www.netlib.org/lapack/
LAPACK     : Linear Algebra Package Fortran Library
             http://www.netlib.org/lapack/
(P)ARPACK  : Parallel Arnoldi Package Library
             http://www.caam.rice.edu/~kristyn/parpack_home.html
XERCES-C++ : XML Parser
             http://xml.apache.org/xerces-c

NEMO3D has been tested with Python version v1.5, v2.1, and v2.2.
Since Python is used for simple expression parsing of the XML input data,
even the older Python v1.5 is sufficient.


NEMO3D is distributed with four external packages:

BLAS       : Version 3.0 + update; May 31, 2000
LAPACK     : Version 3.0 + update;  May 31, 2000
(P)ARPACK  : PARPACK based on ARPACK Release 2.1
XERCES-C++ : Version 2.1.0, General UNIX Source Code build

The packages used in NEMO3D are identical to those available from their 
respective distribution websites. We have simply included them along 
with NEMO3D distribution for user convenience.  

If you are already running your own [optimized] versions of BLAS and LAPACK,
you may delete the "NEMO3D/LAPACK" subdirectory altogether and modify
"NEMO3D/build/make.inc" such stat LIB_BLAS and LIB_LAPACK point to your
BLAS and LAPACK static libraries.  Also, a patch (available at 
ftp://ftp.caam.rice.edu/pub/software/ARPACK) has been applied to the 
version of PARPACK included with this distribution.

If you already have Xerces-C++ installed, or would like to use a newer 
version of Xerces-C++ (when available), then you may delete the 
"NEMO3D/xerces-c-src2_1_0" subdirectory altogether and update the 
environmental variable XERCESCROOT (see below).
However, NEMO3D's XMLtoC component was originally developed using the
DOM and parser models of Xerces-C++ v1.7.0.  Thus, while NEMO3D
is distributed with Xerces-C++ 2.1.0, it uses the now deprecated
v1.7.0 objects which are still distributed with v2.1.0.
Later versions of Xerces, however, are not guaranteed to be compatible
with NEMO3D.



Distribution Structure
======================

The structure of NEMO3D is divided into subdirectories of functional components.


   NEMO3D/

	README              : Text file with general overview information.

	BUILD               : Text file with build instructions.

	LICENSE             : Licensing file for NEMO3D.

	ARPACK              : Contains the Arnoldi-based eigensolver (P)ARPACK

	build/              : Contains the master Makefile and include that 
			      builds all the components together to create 
 			      NEMO3D. The Makefile recursions begin here.

	eigen/              : The Parallel Lanczos Eigensolver component used
			      to solve for eigenvalues.

	LAPACK/             : Contains Netlib's LAPACK and BLAS Fortran 77
			      mathematical routines.

	nemo3d/             : The core of NEMO3D. 

	nml/                : The Nemo Math Library component for mathematical
			      operations.

	xerces-c-src2_1_0/  : The Xerces-C++ v2.1.0 XML Parser distributed from
			      the Apache XML Project.

	XMLtoC/             : The XML to C code generator and XML I/O component
			      used to read in XML data.


Build and Installation
======================

NEMO3D has been tested on two platforms -- x86 running gnu/Linux and
MacOS X.  For build instructions on these two platforms, please see
NEMO3D/build/BUILD. 

NEMO3D does not come with an installation feature. Rather, it simply is
compiled into an executable located in "NEMO3D/nemo3d/bin".


